IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bwa-membership`

-- Bretton Woods Agreements Act 1966, ss 4 to 12 and First and Second Schedules -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_bretton-woods-agreements-act-1966.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `ss 4 to 10 -- who pays`

#ASSERT `who bears the payment` `the IMF subscription` EQUALS `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
#ASSERT `who bears the payment` `charges on special drawing rights` EQUALS `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
#ASSERT `who bears the payment` `a loan or grant supporting a Fund arrangement` EQUALS `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
#ASSERT `who bears the payment` `the World Bank subscription` EQUALS `the Consolidated Fund`
#ASSERT `who bears the payment` `a World Bank par value adjustment` EQUALS `the Consolidated Fund`
#ASSERT `who bears the payment` `interest on a loan raised under section 9` EQUALS `the Consolidated Fund`

#ASSERT NOT `the President must concur` `notes issued to the IMF`
#ASSERT `the President must concur` `notes issued to the World Bank`
#ASSERT `the President must concur` `a loan raised to pay either body`
#ASSERT NOT `the President must concur` `an increase in the IMF quota`

#ASSERT `the Minister for Finance must act or approve` `notes issued to the World Bank`
#ASSERT `the Minister for Finance must act or approve` `a loan raised to pay either body`
#ASSERT `the Minister for Finance must act or approve` `an increase in the IMF quota`

